/// newspeak-spec.pdf 6.3: "Execution of the instance initializer begins
/// with evaluation of the message clause given in the class' superclass
/// clause in the context of i. The superclass' instance initializer is then
/// invoked on o with the resulting message. ... Then, all the slot clauses
/// (6.3.2) given in the class' initializer are executed in the context of
/// i, in the order they were declared. Afterwards, the (possibly empty)
/// statement given in the class' initializer is executed. Finally, i
/// returns o to the primary factory method, which returns it to its
/// caller."
///
/// One line per step, in the order 6.3 gives them: the superclass clause's
/// message before anything of Base runs, the whole of Base's initializer --
/// its slot clause and then its statement -- before Derived's first slot
/// clause, Derived's statement after its slot clause, and the factory's
/// answer last. Each of the five orderings is a separate rule, and a
/// reordering of any pair is silent wrong output at exit status 0.
class Spec63InstantiationOrder = Object new (| t ::= nil. |) (
    class Base withArgument: value = Object new (
        | baseSlot = outer Spec63InstantiationOrder log: 'base slot sees the ', value. |
        outer Spec63InstantiationOrder log: 'base statement'.
    ) (
    ) : ()
    class Derived new = Base withArgument: (outer Spec63InstantiationOrder log: 'superclass argument') (
        | derivedSlot = outer Spec63InstantiationOrder log: 'derived slot'. |
        outer Spec63InstantiationOrder log: 'derived statement'.
    ) (
    ) : ()
    public log: line = ( t show: line; newLine. ^line )
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        t:: platform transcript.
        Derived new.
        t show: 'the factory answered'; newLine.
    )
) : ()
